  "scope": [
    "Product revision fence against inactive identities, tombstones and same-page accepted generations; full-refresh stale row skip accounting.",
    "Stock decimal propagation through catalog, business/shadow reads and writes, local mutation intent/outbox, supplier imports, ProductDB/CSV adapters and editor validation.",
    "CLI and shared PosWorkflowService/harness files: stock type adapters and STOCKUI regression only, not their entire unrelated delta."
  ],
  "resolvedFinding": {
    "problem": "Repository CSV adapter captured omitted stock before obtaining CatalogMutationGate and could overwrite a newer committed stock during a rename.",
    "correction": "The adapter passes preserveExistingStock; LocalProductWriter reads the current quantity after acquiring the gate, inside the same rename transaction. Remote origins reject the local preservation flag.",
    "regression": "CsvAbsentStockConcurrencyTests controls the gate, queues a rename, commits 3.456, releases the gate and verifies rename and quantity after reopen without sleeps."
  },
  "reviewedBoundaries": [
    "Timestamp product revision comparison does not order opaque catalog watermarks; legacy unversioned rows remain compatible.",
    "Full-refresh stale products are skipped before business, shadow, reference and image changes; persisted inactive identities are included in the page fence.",
    "Stock retains decimal fractions. CLP retail/purchase fields and sale-line quantities retain their existing integer types.",
    "Local stock validates nonnegative quantities up to Int32.MaxValue at three fractional digits; import applies its narrower 999999999 backend limit; remote reads preserve additional fractional digits.",
    "Invalid supplied import quantities are row errors; omitted quantities preserve existing stock and new products retain zero default."
  ],
